course: dictionary
lesson: 11586
title: Waiting with excitement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Anticipation is a noun. It is the feeling you have while you wait for something you expect to happen, especially something nice. «The children counted down the days with anticipation before the summer holidays.» Counting the days shows they are waiting and excited, so anticipation means excited waiting.
explain: Anticipation can also mean getting ready for something you expect. «The shop stocked extra bread in anticipation of a busy weekend.» The shop expects lots of customers, so it prepares early.
explain: In sport, anticipation means guessing what will happen next. «The goalkeeper's good anticipation let her move before the ball was kicked.» She read the game and was ready in advance.
fact: Anticipation is a noun, and it means excited waiting, getting ready, or guessing in advance.
fact: «In anticipation of» means getting ready for something you expect, as in «in anticipation of rain».
fact: Useful phrases are «with great anticipation» and «full of anticipation».
fact: Anticipation is the feeling before something happens, so look for clues about waiting, planning or expecting in the sentence.
fact: A goalkeeper with good anticipation moves before the ball is kicked because she has read what is likely to happen.
exercise: «Ella counted the days with great anticipation until her birthday.» What does anticipation mean here? | *Excited waiting for something nice | Forgetting something important | Being very tired | Shouting loudly
exercise: «The farmers covered the crops in anticipation of frost.» What does in anticipation of mean? | Forgetting about the weather | Being angry at the cold | Selling all the crops quickly | *Getting ready for something expected
exercise: «Her anticipation of the kick let her dive the right way.» What does anticipation mean in this sentence? | *Guessing in advance what will happen | Feeling sleepy during the game | Losing the match | Kicking the ball very hard
test: «She was full of anticipation before the school trip.» What does full of anticipation suggest? | Lost in a crowd | Angry about a rule | *Excited and looking forward to something | Bored and tired of waiting
test: Which word is closest in meaning to anticipation when it means expecting something? | *Expectation | Sleeping | Forgetting | Shouting
exam: «He waited with anticipation for the results of the race.» What does anticipation mean in this sentence? | *Excited, hopeful waiting | Reading quietly alone | Calm and sleepy rest | Running away fast
